  "what_is_measured": "interface frame time = Main._process to Main._process; achieved speed = slowest dish's clock over wall time. Every dish is filled to its limit and nutrient/feed set to the setup maxima so populations hold. Speed x10,000, backend Auto (the measured build chose between its CPU and GPU simulations), unless the scenario says forced. Every dish has both husk kinds and starvation on (StartConditions.death_husks, plankton_husks and stationary_phase): the game's defaults. The dishes have no plankton bloom, so plankton husks make nothing here; a death by chance leaves a husk.",
  "commit_base": "the measured build is the game before the pooled world: each dish had a simulation of its own, on the CPU or on the GPU, and at most 20 dishes ran at once",
